Input: {"question": "Which award did Jeanne Maindron receive?", "source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 0, "end": 146, "text": "As the sun set over the rolling hills of the French countryside, Jeanne Maindron sat in her cozy parlor, surrounded by the memories of a lifetime."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 147, "end": 260, "text": "The soft glow of the lamp cast a warm light on the faded photographs and yellowed letters that adorned the walls."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 261, "end": 388, "text": "Her eyes, though clouded by the passing of years, still sparkled with a hint of mischief as she reminisced about the war years."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 389, "end": 565, "text": "It was during those tumultuous times that Jeanne, a young woman with a heart full of courage and compassion, had risked everything to hide Jewish families in her small village."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 566, "end": 675, "text": "She had done it quietly, without fanfare, driven solely by her conviction that every human life was precious."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 676, "end": 868, "text": "The whispers of her bravery had eventually reached the ears of the Swedish government, and in 1947, they had bestowed upon her the highest honor in their land: the Royal Order of the Seraphim."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 869, "end": 980, "text": "Jeanne's thoughts were interrupted by the arrival of her great-niece, Sophie, who had come to visit from Paris."}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 981, "end": 1089, "text": "As they sipped tea and nibbled on delicate macarons, Sophie's eyes wandered to the ornate box on the mantle."}, "D1S9": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1090, "end": 1149, "text": "\"Tante Jeanne, what's the story behind that beautiful box?\""}, "D1S10": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1150, "end": 1182, "text": "she asked, her curiosity piqued."}, "D1S11": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1183, "end": 1291, "text": "Jeanne's eyes misted as she reached for the box, adorned with the emblem of the Royal Order of the Seraphim."}, "D1S12": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1292, "end": 1369, "text": "\"Ah, Sophie, that's a tale for the ages,\" she began, her voice low and husky."}, "D1S13": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1370, "end": 1476, "text": "\"It was a chilly winter morning when the Swedish ambassador arrived at my doorstep, bearing this very box."}, "D1S14": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1477, "end": 1559, "text": "Inside, a letter from the King himself, thanking me for my bravery during the war."}, "D1S15": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1560, "end": 1661, "text": "The Order of the Seraphim, he wrote, was a symbol of Sweden's deepest gratitude for my selflessness.\""}, "D1S16": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1662, "end": 1768, "text": "As Jeanne opened the box, a faint scent of lavender wafted out, carrying with it the whispers of the past."}, "D1S17": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1769, "end": 1890, "text": "Sophie's eyes widened as she beheld the glittering medal, its seraphim wings outstretched, shining like a beacon of hope."}, "D1S18": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1891, "end": 1967, "text": "\"Tante Jeanne, you're a true heroine,\" she whispered, her voice full of awe."}, "D1S19": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1968, "end": 2058, "text": "Jeanne's eyes crinkled at the corners as she smiled, her heart full of pride and humility."}, "D1S20": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2059, "end": 2108, "text": "\"I was just doing what needed to be done, Sophie."}, "D1S21": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2109, "end": 2158, "text": "But I suppose it's nice to be remembered for it.\""}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 0, "end": 60, "text": "**Heroic French Woman Honored for Bravery During Holocaust**"}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 62, "end": 250, "text": "In a remarkable display of courage and humanity, Jeanne Maindron, a French woman, has been posthumously awarded the prestigious title of Righteous Among the Nations by the State of Israel."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 251, "end": 354, "text": "This esteemed honor is bestowed upon non-Jews who risked their lives to save Jews during the Holocaust."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 355, "end": 506, "text": "Maindron's selfless actions during World War II have been recognized and documented by Yad Vashem, the World Holocaust Remembrance Center in Jerusalem."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 507, "end": 695, "text": "According to records, Maindron, a resident of Lyon, France, provided shelter and protection to several Jewish families, including children, who were fleeing persecution by the Nazi regime."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 696, "end": 823, "text": "\"Jeanne Maindron's bravery and compassion in the face of unimaginable danger are a testament to the best of humanity,\" said Dr."}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 824, "end": 876, "text": "Robert Rozett, Director of the Yad Vashem Libraries."}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 877, "end": 1053, "text": "\"Her actions serve as a powerful reminder of the importance of standing up against hatred and oppression, and we are honored to recognize her as a Righteous Among the Nations.\""}, "D2S9": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1054, "end": 1110, "text": "Maindron's heroism was not limited to providing shelter."}, "D2S10": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1111, "end": 1262, "text": "She also assisted in obtaining false identification papers and other essential documents, enabling her Jewish friends to evade capture and deportation."}, "D2S11": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1263, "end": 1374, "text": "Her courageous efforts undoubtedly saved numerous lives, and her legacy continues to inspire generations today."}, "D2S12": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1375, "end": 1553, "text": "\"Jeanne Maindron's story is a shining example of the impact one person can have in the face of overwhelming evil,\" said Rabbi Israel Meir Lau, Chairman of the Yad Vashem Council."}, "D2S13": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1554, "end": 1708, "text": "\"We are grateful for her bravery and selflessness, and we hope that her story will continue to inspire others to stand up against hatred and intolerance.\""}, "D2S14": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1709, "end": 1901, "text": "According to Yad Vashem, since the establishment of the Righteous Among the Nations program in 1963, over 26,000 individuals have been recognized for their heroic actions during the Holocaust."}, "D2S15": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1902, "end": 2013, "text": "Jeanne Maindron's recognition brings the total number of French citizens honored with this title to over 4,000."}, "D2S16": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2014, "end": 2232, "text": "In a world where hatred and intolerance continue to pose a threat, the story of Jeanne Maindron serves as a powerful reminder of the importance of standing up for what is right, even in the face of overwhelming danger."}, "D2S17": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2233, "end": 2347, "text": "Her bravery and selflessness will never be forgotten, and her legacy will continue to inspire generations to come."}, "D2S18": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2348, "end": 2367, "text": "**Data and Facts:**"}, "D2S19": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2369, "end": 2489, "text": "* Over 26,000 individuals have been recognized as Righteous Among the Nations since the program's establishment in 1963."}}, "candidates": [{"candidate_id": "C0", "answer": "Royal Order of the Seraphim", "card_ids": ["d1:c0"]}, {"candidate_id": "C1", "answer": "Righteous Among the Nations", "card_ids": ["d2:c0"]}], "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "d1", "card_id": "d1:c0", "entity": "Jeanne Maindron", "scope": "Award received in 1947", "claim": "In 1947, the Swedish government bestowed upon Jeanne Maindron the highest honor in their land: the Royal Order of the Seraphim.", "answer": "Royal Order of the Seraphim", "quote": "The whispers of her bravery had eventually reached the ears of the Swedish government, and in 1947, they had bestowed upon her the highest honor in their land: the Royal Order of the Seraphim. Jeanne's thoughts were interrupted by the arrival of her great-niece, Sophie, who had come to visit from Paris. As they sipped tea and nibbled on delicate macarons, Sophie's eyes wandered to the ornate box on the mantle. \"Tante Jeanne, what's the story behind that beautiful box?\" she asked, her curiosity piqued. Jeanne's eyes misted as she reached for the box, adorned with the emblem of the Royal Order of the Seraphim. \"Ah, Sophie, that's a tale for the ages,\" she began, her voice low and husky. \"It was a chilly winter morning when the Swedish ambassador arrived at my doorstep, bearing this very box. Inside, a letter from the King himself, thanking me for my bravery during the war. The Order of the Seraphim, he wrote, was a symbol of Sweden's deepest gratitude for my selflessness.\"", "original_document_number": 1}, {"doc_id": "d2", "card_id": "d2:c0", "entity": "Jeanne Maindron", "scope": "Award received", "claim": "Jeanne Maindron was posthumously awarded the title of Righteous Among the Nations by the State of Israel.", "answer": "Righteous Among the Nations", "quote": "In a remarkable display of courage and humanity, Jeanne Maindron, a French woman, has been posthumously awarded the prestigious title of Righteous Among the Nations by the State of Israel. This esteemed honor is bestowed upon non-Jews who risked their lives to save Jews during the Holocaust. Maindron's selfless actions during World War II have been recognized and documented by Yad Vashem, the World Holocaust Remembrance Center in Jerusalem. According to records, Maindron, a resident of Lyon, France, provided shelter and protection to several Jewish families, including children, who were fleeing persecution by the Nazi regime. \"Jeanne Maindron's bravery and compassion in the face of unimaginable danger are a testament to the best of humanity,\" said Dr. Robert Rozett, Director of the Yad Vashem Libraries. \"Her actions serve as a powerful reminder of the importance of standing up against hatred and oppression, and we are honored to recognize her as a Righteous Among the Nations.\"", "original_document_number": 2}], "initial_answers": ["Royal Order of the Seraphim", "Righteous Among the Nations"]}
